      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nIntel XPU CI intermittently fails on image pull (not tests) with\r\n`failed commit on ref ... no such file or directory` — a transient containerd\r\nGC/ingest race triggered by the cleanup right before pull, not a disk issue.\r\nThe existing `flock` only serializes CLI steps, not containerd's background GC.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Add `pull_image_with_retry` (default 5 attempts, backoff) and fail fast so\r\n  `docker create` doesn't trigger a second racing pull.\r\n- Add a short GC-settle wait in `cleanup_docker` before releasing the lock.\r\n- Tunables: `DOCKER_PULL_MAX_ATTEMPTS`, `DOCKER_PULL_RETRY_DELAY`, `DOCKER_GC_SETTLE_SECS`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- `bash -n` passes; verified retry recovers and failed pull aborts cleanly.",
